# Chat-road fill coverage — FIXTURE corpus (authored, not worker data)
#
# One JSON object per line: {"road": "form"|"chat"|"unknown"|null, "filled": [field, ...]}.
# `filled` is sparse: only what is settled is listed. No values, no ids — see
# packages/db/src/chat-fill-coverage.ts for the strict parser and the privacy rationale.
#
# WHAT THIS CORPUS MODELS. The verified baseline (2026-09-17): the chat road deterministically
# settles ONLY trade / experience / current_city / availability, plus a gated model overlay that
# occasionally lands preferred_locations / shift / salary_expected; every other field is
# structurally unaskable there (CHAT_FACT_OWNER = pages). The form road settles its pack and
# marker-page fields, including the Layer A (b)/(c)/(d)/(e)/(f) surfaces when the worker used
# them. Rows with `road: null` model pre-0107 profiles (source IS NULL); the aggregate counts
# them separately and production expects ~0.
#
# Phase 1 (elicitation) does NOT change this file: the corpus is the fixture the ruler is
# demonstrated on. Real fill rates come from a row-per-worker export in the same format.
